'''''Trifolium ornithopodioides''''', or the '''bird's foot clover''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Fabaceae]].<ref>{{cite web |title=''Trifolium ornithopodioides'' bird's foot clover [2] |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/161638/i-trifolium-ornithopodioides-i/details |date=2022 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=26 April 2022 |quote=Other common names; bird's bill, bird's foot [3] }}</ref> It is native to Europe, [[Madeira]], and northwestern Africa, and has been introduced to Australia and New Zealand.<ref name="20010350-1">{{cite POWO |id=20010350-1 |title=''Trifolium ornithopodioides'' L. |access-date=25 April 2022 }}</ref> It is a [[halophyte]].<ref name="1_of_338_Google_Scholar_results">{{cite journal |title=Effects of grazing by horses and/or cattle on the diversity of coastal grasslands in western France |year=2004 |last1=Loucougaray |first1=Grégory |last2=Bonis |first2=Anne |last3=Bouzillé |first3=Jan-Bernard |journal=Biological Conservation |volume=116 |issue=1 |pages=59–71 |doi=10.1016/S0006-3207(03)00177-0 |bibcode=2004BCons.116...59L }}</ref>

